Exact shape to honour:

export interface ResolveOptions {
  readonly kinds?: readonly string[];
  readonly path?: string;
}

export function resolve(source: ResolutionSource, query: string, options?: ResolveOptions): Resolution;

Ambiguous variant gains two fields:
  { status: "ambiguous"; step: ResolutionStep; candidates: ResolutionCandidate[]; candidates_total: number; candidates_shown: number }

Rules:
- path filter = isUnderPrefix(node.file, path) from #shared/paths. Absent, empty or undefined path means no filter, and every existing caller keeps its current answer.
- The filter applies inside every step (exact_qn, exact_name, dotted_tail, path, decorator) AND to near misses, so a filtered query never answers ok from outside the prefix and never lists a near miss from outside it.
- candidates_total = number of tied winners BEFORE the CANDIDATE_CAP slice; candidates_shown = candidates.length. Cap stays 5.
- Every "index+1 of N candidates" text uses candidates_total, so the phrase and the field can never disagree.
- Do not change STEP_SCORE values, the step order, or the scoring model: an ambiguous set must still tie.
- Report/report keys are a public contract: no renames of existing ResolutionCandidate fields.
- Do not touch tests/domain.test.ts cases unrelated to resolution.

Exact shape to honour (new files only; import UnresolvedRef as a type from #shared/store/read/coverage):

export const UNRESOLVED_BUCKETS = ["builtin_stdlib","external_package","internal_module","dynamic_property_call","receiver_type_unknown","ambiguous"] as const;
export type UnresolvedBucket = (typeof UNRESOLVED_BUCKETS)[number];

export const BUILTIN_RECEIVERS: ReadonlySet<string>;
export const BUILTIN_MEMBERS: ReadonlySet<string>;

export function bucketOf(row: UnresolvedRef): UnresolvedBucket;
export function bucketCensus(rows: readonly UnresolvedRef[]): { readonly buckets: Readonly<Record<UnresolvedBucket, number>>; readonly material: number };

Bucket rules, in order:
1. evidence starts with "import:": take the SPECIFIER — the text after the prefix up to the first space, because issue #12 appends competing candidates after a space ("import:./x.js candidates: a.ts | b.ts"). Starts with "./" or "../" or "#" -> internal_module. Starts with "node:" or "bun:" or names a node/bun builtin -> builtin_stdlib. Anything else -> external_package. This rule runs FIRST, deliberately: a bucket names what the specifier is, so a #12 evidence suffix or a changed evidence_kind can never move an import into a different bucket.
2. evidenceKind === "ambiguous" -> ambiguous (whatever the evidence says).
3. evidence starts with "call:": split raw_target at the LAST dot into receiver and member (no dot -> receiver "", member = raw_target). Receiver in BUILTIN_RECEIVERS -> builtin_stdlib. Else member in BUILTIN_MEMBERS -> builtin_stdlib. Else evidenceKind === "dynamic" -> dynamic_property_call. Else -> receiver_type_unknown.
4. Everything else ("inherits", a bare "call"/"import" with no colon) -> receiver_type_unknown.

material is computed from its own predicate, NOT from the bucket name:
  material = count of rows where evidenceKind === "ambiguous" OR bucketOf(row) === "receiver_type_unknown"
Rationale: material answers "could a user-defined symbol be the real target?". TASK-017 makes a relative-import tie record evidence_kind "ambiguous", so those rows become material automatically through this predicate; a "missing_module" row is a broken import, not a hidden caller, and stays non-material.

BUILTIN_RECEIVERS seed: Array, Object, Map, Set, Promise, Date, JSON, Math, String, Number, Boolean, RegExp, Error, console, fs, path, os, process, Buffer, URLSearchParams. BUILTIN_MEMBERS seed: push, pop, shift, unshift, splice, slice, join, map, filter, reduce, forEach, find, includes, indexOf, split, trim, toLowerCase, toUpperCase, toISOString, keys, values, entries, has, get, set, add, delete, existsSync, readdirSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync, mkdirSync, statSync, isDirectory, isFile, resolve, dirname, join, basename. Both are data with a comment stating they are a recall trade-off, not a truth.

The tests must assert the interaction with TASK-017: an import row whose evidence carries a " candidates: " suffix still buckets as internal_module, and an import row with evidenceKind "ambiguous" buckets as internal_module yet counts as material.

Never import from src/tools or src/indexer (shared-isolation).
